  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A trapped beastman Gu Immortal says his entire body is full of food path dao marks at a level none before him reached. He consumes rocks and wind to fill his stomach, eats Gu worms to increase the dao marks on him, and after a thousand years of eating dao marks breaks the agreement that bound him.",
      "chapters": [
        1014
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "General dao marks and attainment levels are covered on dao marks and attainment.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_dao_marks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Even Gu Immortals die if they do not eat, unless they have the relevant food path dao marks.",
      "chapters": [
        1032
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "surviving-without-food",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "You Chan tests copper dragonfish several times and finds them better than ordinary dragonfish because their bodies have a higher proportion of food path dao marks.",
      "chapters": [
        1478
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "dragonfish-quality-test",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_you_chan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Black oil is an immortal material that contains food path dao marks. Once it sticks to a Gu Master, those marks are carved onto the body; conflicting dao marks alone can be fatal, and mortal bodies cannot endure the corrosion.",
      "chapters": [
        1655
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "black-oil-corrosion",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "res_black_oil",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later restates that contact with black oil carves food path dao marks into Gu Masters and weakens oil collectors through conflicting marks.",
      "chapters": [
        1893
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "black-oil-corrosion",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The gluttonous demon frog is a legendary immemorial beast that contains an unimaginable number of food path dao marks. Under those marks, Myriad Beast Fusion Color Heaven lets humans eat Gu materials to increase corresponding dao marks and gradually construct totems with Gu worms there.",
      "chapters": [
        2112
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "totem-construction-method",
